<!DOCTYPE HermitCrabInput SYSTEM "HermitCrabInput.dtd">
<!-- Divergence-001 adversarial grammar G2: "stale branch", a genuine real, forward-synthesizable
     word that Add finds and PriorityUnion LOSES entirely (not merely an extra spurious reading of
     an otherwise-shared word, as in G1: here the two engines disagree on whether "zudiueo" parses
     at all). Also exercises a genuine 3-symbol ("num" = sg/du/pl) multi-bit lane, so the Add-side
     widened value is a real two-value disjunction, never the degenerate "union covers every
     declared symbol so the feature gets deleted" corner case (that corner case is exercised
     separately, deliberately, in G1's 2-symbol cat feature).

     Four suffixes on one root, an unordered stratum (order is disambiguated by construction: each
     rule inserts a distinct, non-overlapping single segment, so only one segmentation of any given
     surface string is ever pattern-matchable):
       mrA  RequiredHeadFeatures num=du, OutputHeadFeatures num=pl.  suffix "i"  (innermost)
       mrB  no RequiredHeadFeatures,     OutputHeadFeatures num=sg.  suffix "u"
       mrC  RequiredHeadFeatures num=sg, OutputHeadFeatures num=pl.  suffix "e"
       mrD  RequiredHeadFeatures num=pl, no OutputHeadFeatures.      suffix "o"  (outermost)
     Root "zud" carries no AssignedHeadFeatures (num unconstrained).

     Forward (root to surface): empty, then mrA (req du, out pl) gives pl, then mrB (no req, out
     sg) gives sg, then mrC (req sg, out pl) gives pl, then mrD (req pl, no out) gives pl.
     "zudiueo" is this real 4-morph word.

     Analysis unapplies outside-in: mrD, mrC, mrB, mrA.
       unapply mrD: fs empty folds to req_D=pl (both modes agree, folding onto empty always
         agrees).
       unapply mrC: check out_C=pl against fs=pl (both pass). Fold in req_C=sg:
         PriorityUnion becomes fs=sg (overwritten).
         Add becomes fs={pl,sg} (union; a real 2-of-3 disjunction, num has 3 declared symbols so
         this is not the "all declared symbols" deletion corner case).
       unapply mrB: check out_B=sg against fs (PriorityUnion: sg vs sg, true; Add: sg vs {pl,sg},
         true: both pass, as they always do for the rule that set the diverging feature).
         req_B is empty, so both modes pass the fs through unchanged: the divergence introduced at
         mrC survives this step untouched.
       unapply mrA (innermost): check out_A=pl against fs.
         PriorityUnion: fs=sg, is_unifiable(pl,sg) is false, so mrA's own gate refuses. The whole
           derivation dead-ends: PriorityUnion finds ZERO analyses of "zudiueo".
         Add: fs={pl,sg}, is_unifiable(pl,{pl,sg}) is true (pl is a live member of the stale
           2-value set left over from mrC, three steps back), so mrA's gate admits. The derivation
           reaches the root and succeeds: Add finds ONE analysis of "zudiueo".

     Controls:
       zud      bare root.
       zudi     mrA alone.
       zudiu    mrA+mrB.
       zudiue   mrA+mrB+mrC, mrD skipped. Negative control: this happens to also be
                forward-synthesizable, but analysis dead-ends identically in BOTH modes (mrD never
                contributed pl to widen anything, so mrA's out=pl vs fs=sg fails for Add too),
                confirming the divergence on zudiueo is attributable specifically to mrD's stale
                contribution, not some general property of this rule shape.
       zudueo   mrB+mrC+mrD, mrA skipped. Non-vacuousness control: the very same override chain
                (mrC writes pl, mrD requires it) succeeds identically in BOTH modes whenever mrA
                (the rule whose own gate is what diverges) is not part of the chain.
       zudiueo  THE bug pin: Add finds 1 analysis, PriorityUnion finds 0. -->
